starwars the rise of Skywalker has the  unenviable task of wrapping up the  latest Star Wars trilogy uniting a fan  base that's become increasingly divided  and concluding the decade spanning so  called Skywalker saga that's a lot for  one film to manage does it pull it off  well yes and no the rise of Skywalker  should have been Leia's movie on solo  got the spotlights in the force awakens  and Luke Skywalker's story dominated the  last Jedi with the rise of Skywalker it  was Leia Stern unfortunately carrie  fisher's tragic death in December 2016  made a big Leia showcase impossible  forcing JJ Abrams to cobble together an  arc for the princess turned general from  old outtakes it's not perfect Leia's  dialogue is noticeably vague and it's  obvious that Abrams is using a stand-in  when Leia space is hidden she doesn't  have any standout moments the climax of  her arc is a little vague and much of  her plotline is carried out by other  people talking about her not what she  actually does however it works pretty  well land it's much bigger than a cameo  Leia is in multiple scenes and she has a  complete arc in the movie obviously it  would have been better if Carrie Fisher  was still around to give lay out the  send-off she deserves  given what Abrams had to work with  though playas final on-screen appearance  is significantly better than we expected  the last entry in the skywalker saga  begins at a breakneck pace and it  doesn't slow down to breathe until the  film's final minutes in order to set up  its end game the rise of skywalker  introduces new characters new planets  new gizmos and new ideas so fast that  it's impossible to keep track of them  all  every new plot thread introduces a dozen  questions at episode 9 simply doesn't  have time to answer well reports differ  depending on who you're talking to it  seems pretty clear that Disney and  Lucasfilm didn't plan this new Star Wars  trilogy out from the beginning in the  rise of Skywalker that decision catches  up with them the first half of the movie  while full of action is mostly set up  for the second half it would have been a  lot better as some of those ideas that  suddenly show up in episode 9 had been  seated throughout the previous two  movies  [Music]  as it is however one film has to do a  lot of heavy lifting and there's not  quite enough room returning characters  like r2d2 and Rose Tico barely make an  impact new characters like dominic  monaghan SPO Mont kin and Naomi a Kees  Janna hardly register at all it all  makes for a very bloated and  unsatisfying viewing experience there's  a version of this movie that's much  tighter but unfortunately it's not the  one we've got you know who steals  practically every single scene he's in  in the rise of Skywalker  c-3po for one Luke's fussy protocol  droid is funny or an episode 9 that he's  ever been  but he also proves surprisingly vital to  the movie story even in a new hope c-3po  is mostly around to translate for r2d2  this time c-3po translation skills are  instrumental in moving the plot forward  if you told us a few years ago that  episode 9 would have a steering up over  c-3po a lifelong comedic relief  character we wouldn't have believed you  and yet here we are did you like the  last Jedi if so sorry  the rise of Skywalker does a very good  job dismantling pretty much everything  that movie put down supreme leader snoke  surly demise as it turns out he wasn't  really that important the near  extinction of the resistance it was only  temporary when we rejoined them they  found a lot of new recruits Rey's  parents well put it this way they were  definitely somebody the rise of  Skywalker buries its predecessor in a  way that feels petty sacrificing lots of  set up and unsatisfying passion  the only thing from episode 8 it really  keeps are the poor's finn rey poe and  kylo Ren are the best things about the  new Star Wars trilogy even when the  script lets them down these actors are  so charismatic that it's fun to just  watch them run around quip bicker and  get into trouble the rise of Skywalker  gives us a lot of that and it's just as  fun as you'd expect  even though finn still doesn't have much  of an arc ultimately though the film  hinges on the relationship between ray  and kylo thankfully Ridley and Driver  are more than up to the task the  chemistry that the duo shared in the  last Jedi is cranked up to 11 here and  the two actors carry the movie given how  bonkers the plot is that's a massive  feat going into the rise of Skywalker  fans had some major questions now that  it's out they still do we never learned  how Palpatine came back to life he just  is raised true nature comes out of  nowhere and isn't adequately explained  and many key plot points are glossed  over completely the movie constantly  tells us that things happened but it  doesn't tell us how or why you may  recall that the force awakens did the  same thing where'd you get that a good  question for another time granted some  of the Disney produced spin-off  materials offer a few clues but viewers  shouldn't have to do extra research to  understand the basic plot of a movie no  matter how much Disney wants that to be  the case JJ Abrams went big with the  rise of Skywalker and if he didn't quite  stick the landing he certainly at least  tried it's a movie that's full of  spectacle the dog fights the lightsaber  duels and the blaster battles are bigger  than anything we've ever seen in a Star  Wars movie before and the Easter eggs  cameos and nods to past Star Wars films  pop up everywhere it's hard to think of  a better tribute to Star Wars especially  given the final scene which takes us  back to where everything began the rise  of Skywalker is bold ambitious  convoluted messy hopeful over odds and  complicated in other words that Star  Wars in a nutshell this is it Luke Leia  Han c-3po r2d2 and Darth Vader are done  for now at least it appears we finally  know how this story ends the same seems  to be true for our new heroes too none  of the main actors involved with the  sequel trilogy seem particularly keen on  coming back for more  and given the rise of Skywalker's  definitive ending it's hard to imagine  that their future adventures will be  quite as exciting as the one that just  concluded true Star Wars isn't going  anywhere  Disney will crank out new material set  in a galaxy far far away for decades to  come still it's just not going to be the  same without our old and newer friends  at the helm thanks for the memories  folks may the force be with you check  out one of our newest videos right here  plus even more looper videos about Star  Wars are coming soon subscribe to our  YouTube channel and hit the bell so you  don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

